  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1709,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\cocoartf949\\cocoasubrtf540\n{\\fonttbl\\f0\\fswiss\\fcharset0 Helvetica;}"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2709,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "{\\colortbl;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\n\\paperw11900\\paperh16840\\margl1440\\margr1440\\vieww20580\\viewh14900\\viewkind0"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3709,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\\pard\\tx566\\tx1133\\tx1700\\tx2267\\tx2834\\tx3401\\tx3968\\tx4535\\tx5102\\tx5669\\tx6236\\tx6803\\ql\\qnatural\\pardirnatural"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4709,
    "dDurationMs": 3251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\\f0\\fs24 \\cf0 Hi, and welcome to Veritasium,\nan online science video blog. I'd like to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7960,
    "dDurationMs": 7270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "take on scientific topics all the way from\nthe simplest to the most complex. So a good"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15230,
    "dDurationMs": 5039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "place to start, I think, is with a problem\nconsidered by the famous physicist Richard"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20269,
    "dDurationMs": 8630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Feynmann. He asked, \"If all the world's scientific\ninformation except for one sentence were destroyed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28899,
    "dDurationMs": 7611,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in some cataclysmic event, which single statement\nwould contain the most scientific information"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36510,
    "dDurationMs": 9799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for future generations?\" His conclusion was\nthat it is The Atomic Hypothesis. [Music]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46309,
    "dDurationMs": 6291,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The atomic hypothesis states that all things\nare made up of atoms, tiny particles that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52600,
    "dDurationMs": 6689,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are in perpetual motion; they attract each\nother when a little distance apart but repel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59289,
    "dDurationMs": 6531,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if squeezed together. That statement is incredibly\nimportant to understand if you want to understand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65820,
    "dDurationMs": 6670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most of the rest of science, because everything\nis made of atoms, including you and me and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72490,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Opera House, and the Harbour Bridge, and\nthe water, and the trees, and the grass, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76840,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the air and the clouds, and, well, you get\nthe idea. Everything is made out of atoms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82100,
    "dDurationMs": 4330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it's really important to understand the\natomic concept if you're going to understand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86430,
    "dDurationMs": 6350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the rest of science. The idea that everything\nis made out of tiny particles has been around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92780,
    "dDurationMs": 6890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for thousands of years. The oldest recorded\ntexts are in Greece and India. In fact the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99670,
    "dDurationMs": 7250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "word atom comes from the Greek atomos, meaning\nliterally, uncuttable. So the idea that they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106920,
    "dDurationMs": 8400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had was if you took a piece of matter, like\nthis piece of aluminium foil, you could cut"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115320,
    "dDurationMs": 10409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it in half\nand in half again each time reducing the number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125729,
    "dDurationMs": 6131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of atoms by half. But the idea was you could\nnot go on doing that indefinitely, for there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131860,
    "dDurationMs": 9300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would come a point when you have only a single\natom left and it is uncuttable, it's an atom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141160,
    "dDurationMs": 5580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How many times do you think I could cut this\nA4 sheet of aluminium in half before I reach"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146740,
    "dDurationMs": 780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a single atom?}"
    } ]
  } ]
}
